      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When creating a master service agreement for a raw material supplier, consider including the following standard terms and conditions to mitigate supply chain volatility and price fluctuations: \n\n1. Price stabilization clauses or ramp-up provisions to lock in prices for a specified period.\n2. Damage assessment and indemification clauses for losses due to supplier-caused disruptions.\n3._quantity discounts and/or price escalation provisions for unexpected increases in raw materials costs.\n4. Minimum order quantity (MOQ) or minimum purchase clauses to encourage regular, predictable buying behavior.\n5. Dispute resolution provisions, such as arbitration clauses or mediation processes.\n6. Payment terms with retention or delayed payment provisions to timewise slice the risk of sudden price fluctuations.",
